<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nasr ibn Ali</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1012/13</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> · Also known as Arslan Ilek Nasr</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nasr ibn Ali was a Kara-Khanid ruler who in 999 captured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bukhara">Bukhara</a> and ended the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samanid-empire">Samanid Empire</a>, bringing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/transoxiana">Transoxiana</a> under Turkic Muslim rule. His conquests made the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kara-khanid-khanate">Kara-Khanids</a> neighbours and rivals of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahmud-of-ghazni">Mahmud of Ghazni</a> along the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oxus">Oxus</a>. His son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ibrahim-tamghach-khan">Ibrahim Tamghach Khan</a> later founded the Western Kara-Khanid Khanate at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samarkand">Samarkand</a>.</p></div>
